From 89e57cce87f7f923dc2e2b4f4d9e58f085ce57d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Hoskinson <charles.hoskinson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:42:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] T10: h_hi 16-bit range table in N1, the bound lfr_call path,
 T10 cases

- stmt.rs: HhiRangeAir (2 columns, 2^16 rows, bus 963) in the N1 layer; the First statement AIR looks up
  each h_hi limb of every enabled row (lead ruling on T7 pick 9).
- t7_chain: `t10 key|args|call` runs the T7 chain of program A or B into the acceptRun ORD call of
  sherlock-ledger.compact, with the ledger anchor operand anchor_d2(r_L, prog_d) and gen_ops_check on the
  L_Fr tape (A_0 = C_P); SHERLOCK_LEDGER_PROG puts another program's anchor in the call (refused at the
  tape, exit 3); T10_PROBE_ONION measures L with the onion AIR against G1.
- cases: changed leaf post_d (public values only, and trace plus public values), h_hi limb of 2^16.
- lfr_call: the T10a command line over the t7_chain T10 path (SHERLOCK_PROG A or B).
